codex
A more substantive variance-reduction idea is to treat the final preactivation as approximately Gaussian: compute its sample mean and variance, then blend the empirical ReLU mean with the closed-form Gaussian ReLU moment. This adds little FLOP cost and is most defensible on the final layer, where each preactivation sums many inputs.
